/*******************************************************************************
*         McXtrace instrument definition URL=http://www.mcxtrace.org
*
* Instrument: ex_battery_mcxtrace_host_starter
*
* %Identification
* Written by: PaNRAID School
* Date: 2026
* Origin: PaNRAID / Battery imaging exercise
* %INSTRUMENT_SITE: Templates
*
* Minimal working host instrument for the McXtrace track of the Li-ion
* battery imaging exercise (../README.md): a plain X-ray source, a
* `sample_pos` Arm declared immediately before the %include, and a flat
* PSD_monitor a short distance downstream. This is the smallest possible
* demonstration of the "connecting point" mechanism described in that
* README - it is NOT a substitute for adapting Airport_scanner.instr from
* $MCXTRACE/examples, which is one of the two build-a-host-instrument
* options in the exercise itself (McXtrace track, step 2).
*
* How this works: everything inside LiIon_Battery_Union_Xray.instr is
* positioned relative to its own `sample_pos` Arm (a REMOVABLE COMPONENT).
* Declaring another component instance also called `sample_pos` here, right
* before the %include line, makes that instance - not the included file's
* own AT (0,0,0) ABSOLUTE placement - the one the battery geometry actually
* attaches to. Move or rotate the `sample_pos` Arm below and the whole
* battery moves with it.
*
* Energy defaults to 60 keV to match the my_absorption placeholders
* documented in LiIon_Battery_Union_Xray.instr's own header (see ../README.md,
* "Pick a beam energy deliberately").
*
* %Parameters
* E0: [keV]              Mean source photon energy
* dE: [keV]               Source energy half-width
* dist_sample: [m]       Source-to-sample distance
* dist_detector: [m]     Sample-to-detector distance
*
* %End
*******************************************************************************/
DEFINE INSTRUMENT ex_battery_mcxtrace_host_starter(E0=60, dE=1,
                                                    dist_sample=5, dist_detector=0.5)

TRACE

COMPONENT origin = Progress_bar()
AT (0,0,0) ABSOLUTE

COMPONENT src = Source_gaussian(E0=E0, dE=dE, focus_xw=0.05, focus_yh=0.05,
                                 dist=dist_sample)
AT (0,0,0) RELATIVE origin

/* This is the connecting point: same name, same trick, as documented in
 * ../README.md. Reposition or reorient THIS Arm (not anything inside the
 * included file) to move the battery around in your own instrument. */
COMPONENT sample_pos = Arm()
AT (0,0,dist_sample) RELATIVE src

%include "../LiIon_Battery_Union_Xray.instr"

COMPONENT det = PSD_monitor(xwidth=0.1, yheight=0.1, nx=200, ny=200,
                             filename="radiograph.dat")
AT (0,0,dist_detector) RELATIVE sample_pos

END
